{"type":"message","id":"cde0f294","parentId":"666a7dd5","timestamp":"2026-03-18T11:41:51.790Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0081f5403a9d22a80169ba8f7c69d48191b280792f418d487e\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABpuo99725Hjs-UxwrzAyy-AO-bEY2ewksaTktitNd1A9Sh7VBJjulmW3JYuU0oakAHQa83DEBT5Z1PV5sqC1jvfnc9YuVa_h5pLN3q-7yVzAEb1dJ64F7jY-eIWVkuOU-n2niFlyNMFcCriqymgAGeKKNTq1yGGgracdogjDfpl6-i5WpakBmuSZKcPz2awje9yrt1wQ6IpUDWoZkfdF_uPp82KZ7Ae-hCJywNIX5NlB7MGWJuUr4ptjkTQRHrJcjCDdoA7p6LB3J5r-xUgE_qOpEsXBHAf2o8KNWKF-bMQOI44cG5EQ6GwpNvaDvSRgA8qSe0hzy80qTsa23WXAtnZv7Jr_JFqxUVnybiWkT0b40fm_0GFS2hX7HaOqfFoYLiXU9FMKuf9FtpeXAx6ajRgTNr7aaPZ5CD9g-0JHleMP0c2xHoed6MWbI004C7J0QKxCjat6KkBuqQDFNvCUVry24aSBPpfk6lA2OBANXJLBb_f0j6DKjYsC4NXW9pV_d2LT2RASqM7wnDRZ_SQxHlDBoKyx0VyoikT8nFGJQxRXYwnfqEN62ulrH3ls7fhai4kDw4yFIIIlV7YSgM8AmxnQ3_w1vf9rDwFNTylexTAQuoLZXHxydB8x_2-c-6XMcSq4htKr7lBCz2XdQyRxFYhDecg-d3q9V5SBD4yKOSKlP-ocKfNKGicZEQjgNYcIUwfc_2e4ZE0shM1Z6qX6kAAC8i1CeZYm9nxgOlt0AHmjfacu6BHNt0uAmpyp6WZQue9uAkjSOxrfWWlvhWVT0F4gIaCTfrxO5dAqctc8W7LAiMvLXigw-q0YD_1xJVcDPRXP36OCvMWUSVKjK4cca5CTrRngf20ngSmlPqNVUgdQtv0Es=\",\"summary\":[]}"},{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] That is important. **Pink urine likely means blood in the urine**, and with your history plus right-sided pain, I’d treat this as **concerning and needing prompt medical review**.\n\nIf the bleeding becomes heavy, you pass clots, cannot urinate, feel faint, or the pain becomes severe, go to urgent care / the ER.\n\n**Question 2/5:**  \nDo you also have **fever, chills, nausea, vomiting, or burning when you urinate**?","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0081f5403a9d22a80169ba8f7d35f481919cb153b49fff7a52\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":23325,"output":125,"cacheRead":8576,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":32026,"cost":{"input":0.0583125,"output":0