{"type":"message","id":"8e75b6e6","parentId":"5537ad8c","timestamp":"2026-03-18T12:42:52.189Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] Pain with urination makes a **urinary tract source** more plausible too, including infection or bleeding from the urinary tract — but with your kidney history, it still needs careful evaluation rather than assuming it is a simple UTI.\n\n**Question 3/5:**  \nIs the right-sided pain **worse with movement, bending, or pressing on the area**, or does it feel more like a **deeper internal ache** that stays there regardless of movement?","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0081f5403a9d22a80169ba9dca0bf08191a6b8f7a5524507d6\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":29588,"output":102,"cacheRead":2560,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":32250,"cost":{"input":0.07397000000000001,"output":0.0015300000000000001,"cacheRead":0.0006399999999999999,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.07614000000000001}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1773837766815}}
