iate attention from an emergency room. I want to make sure that I'm prioritizing safety and well-being, so it's crucial to break away from this and advise seeking professional help right away. This feels important to get right!\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] This is **very urgent**.\n\nA **24 kg weight loss in one month**, ongoing **pink urine/blood**, **inner right-sided pain**, and feeling extremely weak/exhausted are **not safe to monitor at home** with your history. This needs **immediate in-person assessment today — ideally the ER / emergency department now**.\n\n### Why I’m concerned\nThese symptoms can be associated with a **serious kidney/urinary problem**, significant bleeding, infection, worsening kidney function, cancer-related progression, severe dehydration, or other systemic illness. I cannot safely narrow this further over chat.\n\n### Please do this now\n- **Go to the ER now** or have someone take you.\n- **Do not drive yourself** if you feel weak, dizzy, or “like a zombie.”\n- Bring or show:\n  - your history of **right kidney clear cell RCC / nephrectomy follow-up**\n  - **CKD stage 3 / reduced kidney function**\n  - recent **pink urine**\n  - **pain with urination**\n  - **persistent right-sided deep pain**\n  - **24 kg unintentional weight loss in 1 month**\n  - profound exhaustion/weakness\n\n### Go by ambulance / emergency services if\n- you feel faint\n- you are confused\n- the pain becomes severe\n- bleeding increases or clots appear\n- you cannot urinate\n- you develop fever/chills, chest pain, or shortness of breath\n\nI do want one last question only because it affects how urgently you should get help on the way:\n\n**Question 5/5:**  \nAre you **alone right now**, and do you feel **dizzy, faint, confused, or too weak to safely get yourself to the ER**?","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0081f5403a9d22a80169ba9e33eaf88191b9351b6e23ff3cb2\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"op