es. Since they have a CT scan, I could suggest they upload it after the ER visit or now if they want me to review it. However, safety protocols suggest prioritizing urgent concerns first. So, ensuring the user understands the urgency is my main focus here. Let's make sure everything is clear and prioritized appropriately!\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] Bring the **CT scan/report with you to the ER right now** if you can access it quickly.\n\nWhat matters most is:\n- the **radiology report text**\n- the **date of the scan**\n- whether it mentions a **mass, recurrence, obstruction, hydronephrosis, stone, bleeding, lymph nodes, or metastases**\n\n### Best next step\n- **Do not delay leaving** just to type it all out here.\n- If the report is already on your phone, show it directly to the ER team.\n- If it’s easy, bring both:\n  - the **written CT report**\n  - the **image file/disc/link** if available\n\n### Very short sentence you or your wife can tell the ER\n“History of right renal cell carcinoma with nephrectomy follow-up and CKD, now worsening right flank pain, pink urine, painful urination, severe fatigue, and major recent weight loss.”\n\nIf you want, you can **send me the CT report text or a photo of it after you’re on the way / once you arrive**, and I can help explain what it means.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0081f5403a9d22a80169ba9e882cbc81919343ea98af2238f1\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":923,"output":280,"cacheRead":33024,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":34227,"cost":{"input":0.0023075,"output":0.0042,"cacheRead":0.008256,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.014763499999999999}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1773837955005}}
